  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "First to the ball – battle and finish",
  "description": "Two lines, one in each corner at one end, and a coach in front of the goal. The coach plays a medium-paced pass straight out, which is the starting signal. The first two players race for the ball; whoever gets control tries to shoot on the goalkeeper at the other end, and the other tries to win the ball back.\n\nAim for match tempo and a real battle, but within limits so no one gets hurt. Go back along the long sides after the shot. Vary it with lifted passes, or with the players starting on their knees. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "React to the pass – not to the coach's movement."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Shield the ball with your body once you have it."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "If you did not get the ball: never give up, chase back."
    }
  ],
